Test rg53: octal escapes in ascii strings and character constants stop at 7
// 8 and 9 are not octal digits, so they end the escape and are ordinary
// characters. They used to be taken as digits: "\18" came out as 020.
// An ascii string packs 2 bytes per word and ends in a null.
//   "A\18B"   A, code 01, 8 (070), B
//   "A\79B"   A, code 07, 9 (071), B
//   "\101"    three digits, the most an ascii escape takes: A
//   '\17'     a character constant, unchanged: 017
100/
    ascii "A\18B"
    ascii "A\79B"
    ascii "\101"
    '\17'
stop
